        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          The Continuous Blood Pressure Device (CBPD) is a continuous, non-invasive beat-to-beat blood pressure, heart rate and ECG measurement device.  The device used during space flight is known commercially as a Portapres Blood Pressure Monitor.  The Portapres uses a cuff placed on a finger to measure systolic and diastolic arterial pressure waveform ECG and heart rate.   The Portapres has an automatic alarm that sounds whenever pressures exceed designated values.  The Portapres connects to the Extended Data Tape Recorder (EDTR) or the TEAC data recorder.  
<END>
